  "query_preview": "..\nTropical Storm Choi-wan and the monsoon flowing into the south side\nof it are dominating weather in the Marianas tonight, and will\ncontinue to do so through the weekend at least. Guam and Rota will\nalmost definitely be outside the radius of damaging winds, so at this\npoint we're handling them with non-tropical hazards, mainly a Wind\nAdvisory and a High Surf Advisory. This covers winds that are\nsignificant, but not quite damaging, and the surf that will be\ncreated by the fairly high waves from Choi-wan.\n\nThe weather associated with Choi-wan will peak on Friday or Saturday,\nbut will be slow to diminish. The weather may not reach normal levels\nuntil Monday or Tuesday.",
